  again  can you imagine twice in your life to  become a chicken so sad not good biela  anyway i remember saying to my dad in  order for me to do this i'm worried i'm  not gonna have medical insurance  so can you um can you figure out a way  like can your company put me on and he  looked at me and he was like i'll forget  he was like  no  and i was like that felt cold you know  that felt real cold but my dad was like  you want to do this  you have to figure it out  you have to figure this out  and what i wound up doing was  taking some jobs i i had to hustle more  to figure it out  but that lesson was so impactful to me  because ultimately  it was good  he he in that moment  gave me a great compliment he said  you're an adult  i raised you you're capable you got this  you want this  go get it  and that's what i did  now had i been able to lean on him and  say oh let me stay on the insurance a  couple more years a couple more years  couple more years maybe i wouldn't have  gotten that second job  maybe i wouldn't have hustled so much  maybe i wouldn't have uh mastered time  management the way that i did maybe i  wouldn't have gotten into teaching and  figured out a whole bunch of stuff about  myself there maybe i wouldn't be here  but that was essential in that moment  that he treated me like a 20 you know  whatever year old i think i was 20  i think it was 23.  he didn't treat me like 16 year old  because i was 16. and i was trying to do  big girl things and he was saying you  want to do big girl things then you got  to act like a big girl so thank you for  that  um again i'm not saying that parents you  know  can't mail you a birthday card or they  save up money for you and they can't say  listen we worked really hard we say this  for you we want you to have that's not  what i'm saying what i'm saying is in  some of those pivotal moments where  you're young and you're impressionable  it's up to your parents to decide  they're going to treat you like a child  or are they going to treat you like the  adult that you are  so this stuff here again the baby  vacation  i titled this episode last night  corruption of kids because i just feel  like the mistakes that are being made  with respect to adults okay  we've been raised right but the mistakes  that are that are happening with respect  to kids i don't care if it's treating  them like babies for way too long and  they sleep on the couch and they get  lazy and they don't figure out how to  fend for themselves and they don't get  that spark of entrepreneurship because  they can be lazy  and they don't have to or we're talking  about a pfizer trial or we're talking  about you know let's have a drag queen  in every school we'll get to that  tomorrow um i don't care what it is kids  are being sacrificed right now  and they're suffering  they're suffering and we can do  something about it we as adults it's our  job they're not gonna know to ask the  tough questions about a vaccine trial  they're not going to know  to be proactive and and be involved in  the school board and make sure that's  not trickling down into the classrooms  they're not they're not raising  themselves we're raising them so if they  want to be  you know spoiled they're going to try to  get away with what they you know kids we  all try to get away with what we can get  away with so adults  we need a wake-up call this is getting  really serious  and if you i don't care where you are on  the ideological spectrum i don't care  i don't care we all love our kids  my message to you today is ask questions  whatever you think the answer is make  sure that's an answer you're comfortable  with  go up to your kid's school see what's  going on there make sure you're  comfortable and if you're not open your  mouth and if you open your mouth and it  doesn't work pull them out figure  something else out  it's our job to be parents and if we're  not parents the kids suffer if you like  the short clip you can catch another one  here or you can catch the full episode  right here  you

